      "writtenOn": "2024-09-26T23:14:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I figured it wasn\u0027t needed in this Rust API since the `callback: F` closure that we get isn\u0027t a free standing function like it is in the NDK API and the object typically captures which instance it\u0027s created for (the instance is passed into `Accessor::new` along with the callback).\n\nBut I see closures might be copyable/clonable so a caller might want to reuse a single definition and may benefit from the parameter, so I added the use of it! WDYT?",
